# Copy to .env.test and adjust. `npm run test:integration` loads that file
# automatically (see vitest.integration.config.ts) — you do not need to export
# anything by hand. A variable already exported in your shell wins over the
# file, which is how CI injects TEST_DATABASE_URL.
#
# TEST_DATABASE_URL is the ONLY variable you need to set. It is the one piece
# of genuinely machine-specific configuration: substitute your local Postgres
# role. Integration tests REQUIRE a dedicated test DB whose name contains
# "test" — the harness refuses to run otherwise, because it TRUNCATEs every
# table between tests.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://inbox@localhost:5432/inbox_test?schema=public

# Everything else the app needs to boot (JWT_SECRET, WEBHOOK_SECRET,
# HEALTHZ_SECRET, AUTOMATION_SWEEPER_SECRET, AUTH_*, EMAIL_INBOX_DOMAINS) is
# set by the harness itself in test/integration/setup/setup.ts and cannot be
# configured here. Those values are fixtures, not deployment config: no test
# asserts anything about them, so a run whose outcome depends on what an
# operator typed is not reproducible. Setting them in this file has no effect.
